% min x subject to x >= 5, x integer: the optimum is 5, attained by s1.
% The objective is integral, so "better than s1" means x <= 5 - 1 = 4: that is the
% { sol } cutoff d1. Rows derived from it hold only at solutions better than s1, and
% there are none, so d2 = 2*c1 - d1 may state x >= 6, which dominates OBJ >= 5.
% The claimed lower bound 5 does not pass s1, as it must.
VER 1.0
VAR 1 x
INT 1 0
OBJ min 1 0 1
CON 1 0
c1 G 5 1 0 1
RTP range 5 5
SOL 1
s1 1 0 5
DER 2
d1 L 4 OBJ { sol } -1
d2 G 6 OBJ { lin 2 0 2 1 -1 } -1
